<title>UK: Fenchurch pretax profits tumble in year.</title>
<headline>Fenchurch pretax profits tumble in year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr  (pence)		7.4		    vs 15.2</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	  2.75		   vs 5.75</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)  5.5		    vs 8.5</p>
<p> Total revenue	     38.37		  vs 34.03</p>
<p> Pretax			4.78		   vs 8.42</p>
<p> Operating profit	  5.09		   vs 8.16</p>
<p> Exceptional		 1.24		   vs nil</p>
<p> Tax			   1.76		   vs 2.80</p>
<p> Attributable		2.70		   vs 5.45</p>
<p> Pay date		    Mar 7, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date   Feb 4, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - Insurance broker Fenchurch Plc said the results reflect the pressures imposed on the broking sector by the demanding environment of over-capacity and intense competition. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
